<section class="shell band">
  <h1>LPC supervision in Texas</h1>
  <div class="answer">
    <p>Reem Glasco has been a Texas Licensed Professional Counselor Supervisor since 2009.
    Supervision is online and available anywhere in Texas, and includes three individual
    hours and one group hour each month. One spot opens in
      <strong>spring 2027</strong>. Equine-assisted sessions near
    Dripping Springs are optional, and EMDR consultation is free while you are an
    associate here.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a class="cta" href="/contact/">Book a free 30-minute consult</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--night">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>The arrangement, in numbers</h2>
    <dl class="facts">
      <div><dt>Monthly fee</dt><dd>$425</dd></div>
      <div><dt>What that includes</dt><dd>Three individual supervision hours and one group hour each month, four hours in total</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Caseload assumption</dt><dd>Ten or more clients a week</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Format</dt><dd>Online only, statewide in Texas</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Openings</dt><dd>One in spring 2027</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Agency contracts</dt><dd>Three-month contracts for associates inside an agency or group practice, $500 a month</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Placement site</dt><dd>Online only</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Equine sessions</dt><dd>Optional, $60 each, Dripping Springs, Texas</dd></div>
      <div><dt>EMDR consultation</dt><dd>Free individual consults while you are supervised here</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Retreats</dt><dd>Annual mindful trail retreat for associates and therapists</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Consult</dt><dd>Free, thirty minutes, Zoom or phone</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p>Why three individual plus one group: Texas asks for at least four supervision hours a
      month, and no more than half of them may be group. Three and one is exactly four, with
      group at a quarter of the total.</p>
    <p>That meets the floor rather than clearing it, so a missed session is made up inside the
      same month rather than absorbed.
      <a href="/texas-lpc-licensure/">The rules are laid out in full in the licensure
      guide</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--sand">
  <div class="shell">
  <h2>What Texas requires of you</h2>
  <p>The Texas requirements are specific, and the part that trips people up is not the total
  hours. It is the floor on months, the split between direct and indirect, and the group
  supervision cap.</p>
  <dl class="facts">
    <div><dt>3,000 hours</dt><dd>Supervised experience required for full LPC licensure</dd></div>
    <div><dt>1,500 of them</dt><dd>Must be direct client counseling contact</dd></div>
    <div><dt>18 months</dt><dd>The minimum, no matter how fast you accrue hours</dd></div>
    <div><dt>4 hours a month</dt><dd>Minimum supervision, with no more than half in a group</dd></div>
    <div><dt>60 months</dt><dd>When your LPC Associate license expires, without renewal</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a class="cta" href="/texas-lpc-licensure/">Read the full guide</a>
  </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shell band">
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <h2>What supervision here is like</h2>
      <p>Supervision is not a compliance meeting. It is the place you bring the session that
      went sideways, the client you think about on the drive home, and the parts of the work
      that are touching something of your own.</p>
      <p>I work collaboratively, which means I expect you to show up prepared, be honest, and
      tell me when something goes wrong. In return you get someone who will help you build a
      practice, not just log hours: fee setting, caseload shape, online presence, referral
      relationships, and the ethics of all of it.</p>
      <p>The clinical lens is trauma-informed and body-oriented. We will talk about the
      nervous system in the room, yours as much as the client's, and about transference and
      countertransference as information rather than error.</p>
      <h3>You will probably fit well here if</h3>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>You want developmental trauma and C-PTSD work to be a real part of your training.</li>
        <li>You are drawn to NARM, Somatic Experiencing, EMDR, IFS-informed work or Brainspotting.</li>
        <li>You intend to build a private practice, now or eventually.</li>
        <li>You can tolerate direct feedback and want it.</li>
        <li>You are curious about experiential and body-based supervision, including work with
        horses.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Reem's supervision credentials</h3>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>Licensed Professional Counselor Supervisor in Texas since 2009, license 66562</li>
        <li>Over fifteen years working with young adults, individuals and associates</li>
        <li>Clinical Partner at Capital Area Counseling, 2021 to 2025</li>
        <li>NARM therapist, Somatic Experiencing Practitioner, EMDR certified</li>
        <li>EMDRIA Approved Consultant, taking therapists toward EMDR certification</li>
        <li>IFS-informed EMDR, steps one through three completed in 2025</li>
        <li>Brainspotting and BASE-P trained, NVC informed</li>
        <li>Coherence therapy training in 2026</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a href="/about/">Reem's full background</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

