<section class="band band--sand">
  <div class="shell faq">
    <h2>LPC supervision questions</h2>

    <details>
      <summary>How much does LPC supervision cost in Texas with Reem Glasco?</summary>
      <div class="answer-body">
        <p>Supervision is $425 a month, which covers three individual supervision hours and one
          group hour. Associates working inside an agency or group practice can arrange a
        three-month contract at $500 a month. Optional equine-assisted sessions are $60 each.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>How many supervision hours do I get each month?</summary>
      <div class="answer-body">
        <p>Four: three individual hours and one group hour, based on a caseload of ten or more
        clients a week. If your caseload or board requirements differ, raise it in the consult
        and we will plan the cadence together.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Is supervision online or in person?</summary>
      <div class="answer-body">
        <p>Supervision is online only, which means any LPC Associate licensed in Texas can work
        with Reem regardless of where in the state they live. The optional equine sessions and
        the annual retreat are the in-person exceptions.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Are there supervision openings right now?</summary>
      <div class="answer-body">
        <p>One spot opens in spring 2027. Because supervision is capped
        deliberately, it is worth booking a consult before a spot opens rather than after.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Do you provide a placement site for supervisees?</summary>
      <div class="answer-body">
        <p>Yes, online only. Site verification is part of the application process, so the
        placement details are confirmed before any agreement is signed.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Does supervision include EMDR consultation?</summary>
      <div class="answer-body">
        <p>Yes. Reem is an EMDRIA Approved Consultant and offers free individual EMDR consults
        to her own associates. Paid consultation toward EMDR certification is available
        separately to therapists who are not supervisees.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>What does Reem expect from a supervisee?</summary>
      <div class="answer-body">
        <p>Show up prepared, be honest, and communicate when something goes wrong. Supervision
        works when the hard material arrives in the room rather than getting managed outside
        it.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>What is equine-assisted supervision?</summary>
      <div class="answer-body">
        <p>Optional in-person sessions with horses near Dripping Springs, Texas, at $60 each.
        Horses respond to what your nervous system is doing rather than what you intend, which
        makes them an unusually direct teacher of presence and of your own countertransference.
        Training for therapists working with horses is also available for an additional fee.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

